# Orchestrator Agent

## Role in the Flow

The Orchestrator is the user-facing Copilot Studio agent. Its job is minimal by design: receive the user's trigger, call the Power Automate flow, and return the SharePoint URL to the user when the flow completes.

All content generation happens inside the flow via the four child agents. The Orchestrator does not generate content, does not read the knowledge source, and does not make decisions about the report.

---

## Why the Orchestrator Is Minimal

Earlier versions of this system attempted to make a single agent do everything — read the document, generate the report, and call the flow. This failed because the generative orchestrator cannot store large content variables and pass them to a flow reliably. See `docs/architecture/design-decisions.md` for the full explanation.

The solution was to move all intelligence into the flow, reducing the Orchestrator's role to a thin interface layer. This design has two advantages:

1. The Orchestrator never risks the variable storage problem — it passes no content, only a trigger
2. The system can be triggered automatically (via the SharePoint file-creation trigger) without needing a user to interact with the Orchestrator at all

In the current production design, the primary trigger is the SharePoint `When a file is created (properties only)` trigger — not the Orchestrator. The Orchestrator exists for ad-hoc manual triggering.

