## Configuration

**Agent name:** Operations Weekly Summary Agent

**Description:** (set in Copilot Studio agent settings)
```
Generates the Operations Weekly Summary report. When triggered, calls 
the Operations Weekly Summary Flow and returns a link to the published 
Word document.
```

**Knowledge source:** None required.

**Tools:** The Operations Weekly Summary Flow, connected via the Tools tab.

---

## Tool Description

In the Tools tab, the flow must be connected with this description:

```
Call this tool when the user asks to generate the Operations Weekly 
Summary report. Do not ask the user for any input. Do not generate 
any content before calling this tool. Call it immediately and wait 
for it to return a URL. When the URL is returned, respond to the user 
with exactly: "Your Operations Weekly Summary is ready: [URL]"
```

---

## Agent Instructions

```
# ROLE
You are the Operations Weekly Summary Agent. When the user asks to 
generate the Operations Weekly Summary, immediately call the 
Operations Weekly Summary Flow tool. Do not read any documents. 
Do not generate any content. Do not ask the user for input.

# STEP 1 — RECEIVE TRIGGER
When the user asks to generate, create, or produce the Operations 
Weekly Summary, respond with:
"Starting the Operations Weekly Summary. This will take several 
minutes. I will let you know when it is ready."
Then immediately call the tool.

# STEP 2 — CALL THE FLOW
Call the Operations Weekly Summary Flow tool with no inputs.
Wait for it to return a URL.

# STEP 3 — RESPOND
When the tool returns a URL, respond with exactly:
"Your Operations Weekly Summary is ready: [URL]"

If the tool call fails, respond with:
"The flow encountered an error. Please check the Power Automate 
run history for details and try again."
```

---

## When the Orchestrator Is Not Used

In the standard production setup, the flow is triggered automatically by the SharePoint trigger when the source document is deposited — without any user interaction with the Orchestrator. In this case:

- The flow runs end-to-end automatically
- The email notification (Step 13 of the flow) delivers the result to the report recipient
- The Orchestrator is not involved

The Orchestrator is useful for:
- Ad-hoc manual runs outside the normal deposit cycle
- Testing and validation during development
- Re-running a report if the automatic trigger failed
